302 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 155 0 R
/E (The best result came from alternating odd layers [1,3,5,7,9] at 84.32% BERTScore, which worked because frozen layers between trained ones prevented gradient interference and allowed each trained layer to specialize cleanly. More surprisingly, training just Layer 1 alone only 4% of the model  achieved 84.19% BERTScore, because adapting the first transformation applied to input tokens creates a legal vocabulary lens that silently improves all 21 downstream frozen layers. Meanwhile, training 10 consecutive layers produced the worst generalization despite the highest training accuracy, confirming that more parameters cause more memorization, not more learning. )
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
